Subject: [PATCH] soundwire: mediatek: Surface Laptop Ultra machine entry (BLOCKED on kernel source)

The soundwire-mtk machine-table entry for the SLU codec layout (2x RT1320
+ RT721 on SDW0) targets drivers/soundwire/mediatek/mtk-sdw-mach.c, which
does NOT exist in the vanilla 7.3.1 tree — it comes from Omarchy's
linux-omarchy kernel (NVIDIA MT8901 series, 1030-n1x-audio.patch).

STATUS: intentionally a no-op marker. Until this flake adopts the Omarchy
kernel or vendors the MediaTek soundwire driver, this "patch" is skipped
(patch -p1 on a nonexistent file fails; the kernel package would abort).
The SLU speaker/jack/mic audio therefore does NOT work with vanilla
nixpkgs 7.3.1 — track via the kernel-source decision in the host config.

